KEY FEATURES
━━━━━━━━━━━━

✓ Real-time frame streaming from FreeBSD guest
✓ Zenoh pub/sub transport (zero-copy, Cap'n Proto)
✓ Local TCP and SSH tunnel support
✓ Automatic PPM → PNG conversion for macOS QuickLook
✓ Cross-platform (macOS, Linux)
✓ Minimal dependencies (Python 3.8+, zenoh, pillow)
✓ Comprehensive documentation
✓ Debugging tools included

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

QUICK START
━━━━━━━━━━━

1. Read first:
   cat /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/00-START-HERE.md

2. Install dependencies:
   bash /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/setup.sh

3. Start broker (on FreeBSD guest):
   ssh -p 2222 -i /srv/bsdos/bsdos-key freebsd@localhost
   su -m root -c '/opt/proto-src/broker/target/release/broker'

4. Run viewer (on Mac):
   cd /srv/bsdos/mac-companion
   python3 display-viewer.py

5. Frames appear → ✓ Success

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

USAGE EXAMPLES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Local viewing:
  python3 /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/display-viewer.py

With SSH tunnel (recommended for remote):
  /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/display-stream.sh --tunnel

Direct to remote broker:
  /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/display-stream.sh --peer tcp/192.168.1.100:7447

Debug Zenoh topics:
  python3 /srv/bsdos/mac-companion/zenoh-inspect.py

