ARCHITECTURE
━━━━━━━━━━━━

FreeBSD Guest               Mac / Linux
┌──────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────┐
│ HAL/Display      │       │                     │
│ /dev/fb0         │──────→│ display-viewer.py   │
│ framebuffer      │ Zenoh │ • TCP 7447 (Zenoh)  │
│ 30 FPS           │ TCP   │ • QuickLook preview │
└──────────────────┘ (SSH  │ • PNG files saved   │
                      tunnel) └─────────────────────┘
Broker: /opt/proto-src/broker/target/release/broker
Topic: bsdos/display/frame (Cap'n Proto frames)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ZENOH_PEER=tcp/localhost:7447     # Broker endpoint
SSH_USER=freebsd                   # SSH username
SSH_HOST=localhost                 # SSH hostname
SSH_PORT=2222                      # SSH port
SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/bsdos-key          # SSH private key

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Minimum:
  Python 3.8
  macOS 10.13 or Linux
  512 MB RAM
  TCP/7447 network access

Recommended:
  Python 3.10+
  macOS 12+ or Ubuntu 20.04+
  2+ GB RAM
  1+ GB disk (for frame cache)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TROUBLESHOOTING
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Problem: "Failed to connect: tcp/localhost:7447"
Fix:     Broker not running. Start: make vm-start && make vm-ssh
         Then: su -m root -c '/opt/proto-src/broker/target/release/broker'

Problem: "No frames received in 10s"
Fix:     Check if display driver is publishing:
         python3 zenoh-inspect.py --follow bsdos/display/frame

Problem: "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'zenoh'"
Fix:     pip3 install eclipse-zenoh pillow

Problem: "SSH tunnel: Connection refused"
Fix:     VM may not be running. Check: make vm-status

See README.md#troubleshooting for more detailed help.

